@startuml
title: VMware FT - Network Transmit Batching Sequence

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Guest OS (in Primary VM)" as GuestOS
participant "Primary Hypervisor" as Primary
participant "Backup Hypervisor" as Backup
participant "Physical Network" as Net

' The Guest OS tries to send data, which traps to the hypervisor.
GuestOS -> Primary: Application issues send() call
activate Primary
Primary -> GuestOS: **Trap:** Pause Guest OS execution
deactivate GuestOS

group Hypervisor Batching Process (Single Trap)

    note over Primary: 1. Places packet data in a temporary
**Transmit Queue**.

    note over Primary: 2. **Batches:** Pulls additional queued packets
from Guest OS network buffers.

    Primary -> Backup: 3. **Logs** the entire batch over the
logging channel.
    activate Backup
    Backup --> Primary: 4. **Acknowledges** receipt of the log.
    deactivate Backup

    note over Primary: 5. **Output Rule Satisfied:**
Sends the full batch to the network.
    Primary -> Net: Transmit Batch of Packets
    activate Net
    Net --> Primary: (Data sent)
    deactivate Net

end

' After the batch is sent, the hypervisor resumes the Guest OS.
Primary --> GuestOS: 6. **Resume** Guest OS Execution
deactivate Primary
activate GuestOS

@enduml
